    "tagline": "Twelve weeks. Four days. Zero guesswork.",
    "description": "A 12-week body-part split built the old way and programmed the new way: the same first lift for every muscle all twelve weeks, three 4-week phases that walk reps from 12-15 down to a heavy 3-5 finish, and every fourth week pulled back on purpose.",
    "coaching_notes": "Primaries never change — that is the point. Log the same lift for twelve weeks and watch the bar load climb. Rest-pause and drop sets appear only on weeks 1-3 of the first two phases; deload and test weeks run clean.",
    "science_overrides": {
      "rep_floor": 3
    },
    "source_provenance": {
      "inspiration": "classic body-part split era",
      "rebuild": "own-brand, Tandem-authored",
      "authored": "2026-07-24"
    }
  },
  "principles": [
    {
      "principle_key": "rep_floor",
      "claim": "A final-phase 3-5 rep strength block is legal inside a build_muscle (hypertrophy) program, deviating from the D10 band floor of 6.",
      "rationale": "Phase potentiation: after eight weeks of 12-15 and 9-11 hypertrophy work, a short heavy block converts accumulated volume into expressible strength and feeds the week-12 realization test. Scoped to primary lifts in phase 3 only; accessories stay at 6-8.",
      "source_citation": "VERIFIED 2026-08-15 against repo research. PRIMARY: 'research-report (8).pdf' PDF page 10, Section 6 (Skill Level Progressions) > Intermediate > 'Periodization Example [5][6]' names this exact structure — 'Mesocycle 1 (Hypertrophy Phase): 4 weeks at 8-12 reps, RPE 7-8' followed by 'Mesocycle 2 (Strength Phase): 4 weeks at 3-5 reps, RPE 8-9', then a deload. Refs [5] traineracademy.org Ch.18 Periodization, [6] NASM blog Periodization Training Simplified. Brick by Brick is difficulty=intermediate, which is the skill level that example is scoped to. SUPPORTING: same report PDF page 6, Section 3 (Rep Ranges by Goal) — 'rep ranges from 5-30 produce equivalent hypertrophy when volume is equated and sets approach failure [13]', and 'the traditional hypertrophy zone (6-12 reps) is empirically validated but not mechanistically unique [15][16]', so the D10 floor of 6 is a conservative default rather than a mechanistic boundary. Also PDF page 13, Section 7 stall management, treats 3-5 as a rep range a programmed lifter legitimately occupies ('stuck at 3-5 reps -> shift to 6-8 for 4 weeks, then return'). SCOPE NOTE: the research licenses 3-5 as a STRENGTH-PHASE mesocycle, not as hypertrophy work — which is exactly how this program uses it. Verified by running the seed: in block 3 the 3-5 range is attached ONLY to the 4 primary_compound slots; secondary_compound and accessory stay at 6-8 and core at 8-10, so no accessory volume drops below the D10 band. SUPERSEDES the prior UNVERIFIED marker, whose claim that 'no repo source names a 3-5 block inside hypertrophy programs' was itself wrong. Originally approved by Kerwin 2026-07-24 (EPIC-031 plan §5 + D16 Notion page 3a7ca37f935b81ce8e88dff8a505fb12)."
    }
  ],
